summary:
I fixed the one defect in PR I-4 and folded the fix into the PR's single commit, keeping its subject. Nothing is pushed. Worktree: /Users/mattogrady/.local/src/worktrees/gglib/lane-remote/gglib.

The resume comment in /Users/mattogrady/.local/src/worktrees/gglib/lane-remote/gglib/crates/gglib-app-services/src/remote/serve_switch.rs (lines 146-151) now reads:

  // No pairing code is minted here, and `resume_arm` is what
  // guarantees it: it passes `Offer::Silent` whatever the request
  // says, so no stored flag can open a live two-minute code at boot,
  // which nobody would read, on an endpoint key a restart does not
  // change. Devices already paired hold a key and need no code; a new
  // one is added with `gglib remote invite`.

I checked each clause against the code:
- **`Offer::Silent` whatever the request says:** serve_switch.rs:174 passes `Offer::Silent` as a literal. `turn_on` and `arm` never read `request.invite`; its only reads are serve.rs:69 and serve.rs:81, both in `enable`.
- **Silent mints nothing:** serve_arm.rs:190-191.
- **Two minutes:** `PAIRING_TTL` is `Duration::from_secs(120)` (pairing.rs:19).
- **Nobody would read it:** `resume_arm` drops the `Enabled` with `.map(|_| ())` (serve_switch.rs:175-176), and `resume` only logs.
- **At boot:** the only boot caller is `remote.resume()` at gglib-axum/src/daemon/mod.rs:212. The one `enable` caller is the HTTP handler at gglib-axum/src/handlers/remote/mod.rs:31.
- **Paired devices need no code:** `arm` seeds every key the roster lists (identity.rs:26-27 and the seeding in serve_arm.rs).
- **`gglib remote invite`:** it exists as `RemoteCommand::Invite` (gglib-cli/src/handlers/remote/mod.rs:50).

The commit message's list of stale sentences now includes: "the resume comment in serve_switch.rs said enable mints a pairing code unconditionally, and enable mints one only when the request asks for an invite". The base comment at a573b639 did say "unconditionally". I amended with `-F msg.txt --cleanup=whitespace` and read the message back; it matches the file byte for byte. No line starts with `#`, and the trailer grep prints 0.

The diff from the old head (d5887529) to the new head touches only those 6 comment lines in serve_switch.rs, so "Comment lines only" in the message still holds. None of the history markers are reintroduced ("no longer", "used to", "previously", "superseded").
